## DECIDE FIRST

**D1. A third owner holds the two-tier name binding, named `NameBinding` (`analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers/NameBinding.cs`).** Responsibility: given a name the source wrote, return the symbol it binds to and the type it denotes, recovering the type from the node's type information when binding fails. Both `AttributeIdentity` and `WrittenNameScanner` call it. PICK: approve — measured below, the two callers need byte-identical mechanics.

**D2. The written-name lens is `WrittenNameScanner` (`WrittenNameScanner.cs`)** — the contract reserved this name for DESIGN ("DESIGN names that second file and brings its name and responsibilities for approval"). Third sibling of `MemberUseScanner` (member uses) and the contracted `DeclaredTypeScanner` (carried types). PICK: approve.

**D3. Documentation references are excluded by a `CrefSyntax` ancestor test, owned by `WrittenNameScanner`.** Cost, stated plainly: inside the gated compilations a doc comment may name any guarded type or member freely — `<see cref="…"/>`, `<seealso>`, `<exception>`, `<inheritdoc cref>` — from any method, including a decoy. No rule any longer proves documentation stays off a forbidden path. PICK: accept the cost; it is what preserves the three live links unchanged. The three production doc comments are **not edited** — the last round's `<c>…</c>` rewrite is withdrawn.

**D4. Surfaces additions.** Production: `NameBinding.cs`, `WrittenNameScanner.cs`, and `AttributeIdentity.cs` (edited — it loses its two-tier body). Tests: `NameBindingTests.cs`, `WrittenNameScannerTests.cs`, `DeclaredTypeScannerTests.cs`, `AnalyzerSourceModel.cs`, `SharedLensOwnershipTests.cs`, `BoundaryRuleWiringTests.cs`.

**D5. One decoy CALL-SITE fixture joins the AG0040, AG0023 and AG0029 test sets.** Acceptance 3 and 5 build decoy CALLEES only. Measured below: a name-only caller check passes every contracted fixture. PICK: yes.

