## 1. MEASUREMENTS — Roslyn 4.14.0.0, throwaway project at `/private/tmp/agentguard-probe-resolution-docs-22665`, outside the repository

Run through the real driver (`CompilationWithAnalyzers.GetAnalyzerDiagnosticsAsync`) except where noted.

**(a) The two callers need identical resolution mechanics.** For `[Guarded(1)]` the attribute's written name binds to `Method:N.GuardedAttribute.GuardedAttribute(int)/Constructor` — not to the type. For `[Guarded]` with the required argument omitted (CS7036) `GetSymbolInfo` yields `null / CandidateReason=OverloadResolutionFailure` while `GetTypeInfo` yields `NamedType:N.GuardedAttribute`. **Both answers are byte-identical whether the `AttributeSyntax` or its `.Name` node is passed.** The written-name lens meets the same two shapes: an attribute name binds to the constructor, so a consumer testing `symbol is ITypeSymbol` misses every guarded type used as an attribute.

**(b) Tier 2 must run only when tier 1 binds NOTHING.** `new Guarded().Field` → `GetSymbolInfo` = `Field:N.Guarded.Field`, `GetTypeInfo` = `int`. A parameter `a` → `Parameter:int a` / `int`. If the recovery ran after a successful bind, a member reference would be attributed to the member's own type at the member's location.

**(c) The error-type filter is load-bearing for the general lens, not only for attributes.** `nameof` → symbol null, `GetTypeInfo` = `?/Error`. `Missing.Thing()` (CS0103) → symbol null, `GetTypeInfo` = `?/Error`. `CrossPlatformAdapters` under CS0246 → symbol null, type filtered to null.

**(d) The denoted type is `ITypeSymbol`, not `INamedTypeSymbol`.** `var arr = new Guarded[1];` — the `var` node's tier-1 symbol is `ArrayType:N.Guarded[]`. Narrowing to `INamedTypeSymbol` in the shared owner silently drops array and pointer coverage.

**(e) The `IAliasSymbol` arm is dead.** An alias use (`AliasG x`) binds straight to `NamedType:AgentGuard.CrossPlatform.CrossPlatformAdapters`; `GetAliasInfo` is the separate accessor. `global::` binds to `Namespace:<global namespace>`. No measured position returns an `IAliasSymbol` from `GetSymbolInfo`, so that arm is not written.

**(f) Namespace symbols leak into a naive consumer.** Reproduced: an AG0041-shaped lens reported `AgentGuard` and `Engine` from `using AgentGuard.Engine;` because a namespace symbol carries a non-null `ContainingAssembly`. The scanner drops `INamespaceSymbol` before dispatch.

**(g) The driver visits crefs, and they resolve.** `RegisterSyntaxNodeAction(IdentifierName, GenericName)` fires inside documentation trivia. `<see cref="SystemServices.Create"/>` is two nodes: `SystemServices` (parent `QualifiedCref`) and `Create` (parent `NameMemberCref`).

**(h) `CSharpParseOptions.Default.DocumentationMode` is `Parse`, and crefs bind under it.** `AnalyzerRunner` calls `CSharpSyntaxTree.ParseText(source)` with no options (`AnalyzerRunner.cs:54, :90, :124`). Measured: `mode=None` → 0 `CrefSyntax` nodes, 1 analyzer hit; `mode=Parse` → 1 cref node, 2 hits; `mode=Diagnose` → same as Parse. **So the documentation tests exercise the real behaviour through the unchanged `AnalyzerRunner`** (Acceptance 18 preserved, no new expected-compiler-error exception). The real build runs `Diagnose` (`Directory.Build.props:37` `GenerateDocumentationFile=true`), where a broken cref is CS1574 — a warning, an error under `TreatWarningsAsErrors` (`Directory.Build.props:36`).

**(i) Crefs produce no operations.** With all five `MemberUseScanner` kinds registered over a file containing two crefs and three calls, exactly the three calls fire. The exclusion belongs to the written-name lens alone; AG0040 (member-use only) is untouched.

**(j) `GetEnclosingSymbol` at a cref position yields the containing TYPE.** `<see cref="Guarded"/>` on `Create()` → `NamedType:SystemServices`. So the cref inside `Create()`'s own doc comment is not "directly inside `Create()`" and IS reported without the exclusion — confirmed end to end: the AG0023-shaped Engine gate reports **3** diagnostics with the exclusion off and **2** with it on, the two being the real code references in a non-`Create` method.

**(k) `ContainingSymbol` cannot satisfy Acceptance 12; `GetEnclosingSymbol` can.** Same call written directly in `Create()`, in a lambda, in a local function: `SyntaxNodeAnalysisContext.ContainingSymbol` = `Method:Create/Ordinary` in all three; `GetEnclosingSymbol` = `Create/Ordinary`, `/AnonymousFunction`, `ViaLocal/LocalFunction`.

**(l) `ILocalSymbol.ContainingSymbol` agrees with `GetEnclosingSymbol` on every local site** (direct `Create/Ordinary`, lambda `/AnonymousFunction`, local function `ViaLocal/LocalFunction`, other method `Other/Ordinary`), and disagrees with `OperationAnalysisContext.ContainingSymbol` for the lambda and local-function cases. A field/property/method declaration's `ContainingSymbol` is the containing **type** — so those declarations are structurally never "inside `Create()`", and the carried-type lens needs no semantic model to answer the caller question.

**(m) `SymbolKind.Method` fires for `get_Prop`.** AG0006's accessor filter (`ContractConcreteTypeMustNotBeReferencedAnalyzer.cs:77-82`) is load-bearing lens mechanics, so it moves into `DeclaredTypeScanner` with the registrations.

**(n) A decoy caller defeats a name-only check.** Three fixtures, each calling `CrossPlatformAdapters.Create()` from a `SystemServices.Create()`: right namespace + right assembly; namespace `Other.Place` in assembly `AgentGuard.Engine`; namespace `AgentGuard.Engine` in assembly `AgentGuard.Engine.Extras`. Identity-checked (assembly + namespace + type name + static + method name): **0 / 1 / 1**. Name-only (`ContainingType?.Name == "SystemServices"`, method `Create`, static): **0 / 0 / 0**.

**(o) Pointer coverage needs no unsafe source and no runner change.** `Compilation.CreatePointerTypeSymbol(t)` succeeds for both a struct and a class target; the `TypeTree.Any` walk finds the leaf through the pointer and through an array-of-pointer (`TypeTree.cs:41-42`).

**(p) Live registration inventory, re-derived this round.** `SyntaxKind.IdentifierName|GenericName|QualifiedName|TypeOfExpression` in `analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers/`: **zero**. `OperationKind.VariableDeclarator`: **one**, `ContractConcreteTypeMustNotBeReferencedAnalyzer.cs:52`. Declaring types registering {Field, Property, Method} together: **one**, the same file. Four types register exactly two of the three — `NoCoverageOptOutAnalyzer` (Method+Property), `NoStateInNativeOpsAnalyzer` (Field+Property), `NoStaticServiceHolderAnalyzer` (Field+Property), `ReturnTypesMustNotBeTuplesAnalyzer` (Method+Property). `ContainingSymbol` reads: **seven**, all flowing into `CompositionPoint` or `OwnerClass` (`TempRootBackDoorAnalyzer.cs:92`, `GuardedConstructionAnalyzer.cs:127/137/151`, `TimeMustUseTimeProviderAnalyzer.cs:71`, `PresenceCheckOnlyFromApprovalGateAnalyzer.cs:82`, `OwnerClass.cs:36`). `GetEnclosingSymbol`: **zero**. `TypeTree.Any` callers: **two**, unrelated (`ContractPattern.cs:50`, `ReturnTypesMustNotBeTuplesAnalyzer.cs:131`). `GetTypeInfo` call sites: **two** — `AttributeIdentity.cs:69` and `NativeCallbackBodyMustBeGuardedAnalyzer.cs:251` (a catch-clause type, single-tier, unrelated). `CrefSyntax` / `DocumentationCommentTrivia` / `IsPartOfStructuredTrivia`: **zero anywhere**.

