## 4. THE THREE LENSES

**`MemberUseScanner` — retained, zero edits.** Five `IOperation` kinds (`MemberUseScanner.cs:29-34`), the per-assembly gate (`:61`), the display text (`:82`). Consumed by AG0040 (Engine gate), AG0041 (both consumer gates), AG0023/AG0029 (their existing Boundaries gate plus one new Engine gate each). It needs no cref exclusion (i).

**`DeclaredTypeScanner` — extracted from AG0006's four registrations.**

```csharp
internal readonly struct DeclaredTypeUse
{
    internal ITypeSymbol Type { get; }        // the declared type to judge
    internal Location Location { get; }       // where to report
    internal ISymbol Declaration { get; }     // the field, property, method, parameter or local
    internal Action<Diagnostic> Report { get; } // SymbolAnalysisContext and OperationAnalysisContext share no base
}

internal static class DeclaredTypeScanner
{
    internal static readonly ImmutableArray<SymbolKind> DeclarationKinds =
        ImmutableArray.Create(SymbolKind.Field, SymbolKind.Property, SymbolKind.Method);

    internal static void Register(CompilationStartAnalysisContext context, Action<DeclaredTypeUse> inspect);
    internal static void RegisterForAssembly(
        CompilationStartAnalysisContext context, string assemblyName, Action<DeclaredTypeUse> inspect);

    // The judgment, pure and directly callable — what the direct scanner tests drive.
    internal static IEnumerable<DeclaredTypeUse> CarriedTypes(ISymbol declaration);
}
```

Extracts verbatim from `ContractConcreteTypeMustNotBeReferencedAnalyzer.cs`: the four registrations (`:49-52`), `field.Type` (`:58`), `property.Type` (`:67`), `method.ReturnType` (`:84`), `parameter.Type` (`:89`), `declarator.Symbol.Type` (`:98`), the implicit-declaration and accessor/event-kind filters (`:77-82`, load-bearing per (m)), and `ReportFirst`'s `locations[0]` choice (`:104-110`). AG0006's `Initialize` becomes one `RegisterCompilationStartAction` line and its diagnostics stay byte-identical (Acceptance 13). Reuses `OwnerClass.InAssembly` for the gate. `TypeTree.Any` stays OUT — each consumer passes its own leaf test, because `TypeTree.Any` has two live unrelated callers and no rule may claim it.

There is no `SemanticModel` in `DeclaredTypeUse`: by (l) only a local can be inside `Create()`, and `Declaration.ContainingSymbol` answers that without a model.

**`WrittenNameScanner` — new, section 2.**

**Consumer leaf test, one shape in all three rules:** judge `Type` through `TypeTree.Any(use.Type, leaf)` when it is non-null; otherwise judge `Symbol.ContainingType` when `Symbol` is a member. Never judge a symbol's `ContainingAssembly` without switching on kind first (f).

